# apps/client — Minute
#
# Every variable here is NEXT_PUBLIC_, and that is the point rather than an
# oversight: this app holds no secret at all. There is no service-role key here
# and there must not be — it bypasses RLS, and every tenancy guarantee Minute
# makes is an RLS policy, so one key in one server action would make the whole
# hardening migration decorative. The privileged insert the invite flow needs
# comes from a SECURITY DEFINER function instead, whose body is readable in a
# migration diff. `lib/boundary.test.ts` asserts the string never appears in a
# source file.

# Supabase — required. Anon key only; the cookie-authed clients in
# lib/supabase/ and the middleware all read these two, and RLS does the rest.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Privacy policy URL — required in any environment where the disclosure gate is
# meant to open. It is the one Service Statement variable with no home in
# `company_profile` (source: 'manual' in the variable schema), because the page
# it points at is a commitment that a page exists rather than a fact about the
# company. The seeded statement cites it, and `resolveDocument` treats an empty
# string as missing and refuses to render the whole body — so leaving this
# unset presents as "The Service Statement is not available" and nobody gets
# past /disclosure. Verify the page is live before the statement goes active.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL=https://your-domain.example/privacy

# Site URL — the origin every magic link redirects back to: ordinary sign-in
# (app/actions/auth.ts) and invitations (app/actions/invite.ts) both read it,
# via lib/siteUrl.ts. Defaults to https://minute.btreasury.com.au, so an unset
# value in local dev mails you a link to production — set it to your dev origin
# to exercise either flow locally. The origin is decided when the mail is sent,
# not when the link is clicked, so the callback's request cannot supply it.
# Whatever you set must also be registered as a Supabase Auth redirect URL, and
# without a trailing slash: GoTrue matches redirect URLs exactly.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
